<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices fall on poor buying.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices fall on poor buying.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Thursday were down in central Indian market due to poor buying support from soybean processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Plants cut their buying prices by 100 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>The monsoon is spreading in Madhya Pradesh gradually, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also down by 100 rupees per tonne on lack of buying support. Undertone was weak.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were down sharply with soymeal yellow at $300 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports in export. Rapeseed extraction was $110 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,800-3,850 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition.</p>
